# HTTPS in front of the Macpardy buzzer server (#103). Caddy gets and renews a
# Let's Encrypt certificate for the domain, upgrades WebSockets on its own,
# and sets X-Forwarded-For to the phone's address.
#
# With MACPARDY_DOMAIN=localhost, Caddy uses its own local certificate
# instead, which is handy for trying the setup on one machine.

{$MACPARDY_DOMAIN} {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy buzzer:8472
}
